@tyouter/dsh-notes README · dsh-notes：`@tyouter/dsh-notes` 1.1.2 — a notebook inside DeepSeek Harness, in three tabs. Type into one box,
read the typeset result beside it, and call the model only when judgement is needed. See
[CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for what the first official release contains.

@tyouter/dsh-notes README · then install the directory through Plugin Manager / install_bundle：```

Requirements: a DSH build with `node:sqlite` (Node 24 ships it). No other runtime dependency is
installed; everything under `lib/` is first-party.

@tyouter/dsh-notes README · The four actions：Capture also works outside the panel: `Alt+N` or the small notebook icon in the
composer tool row opens a floating capture card, and `/note 内容` saves a note
straight from the chat box.

@tyouter/dsh-notes README · Three AI surfaces, three different mechanisms：The panel only creates the session (`POST /notes/api/session/create`) and
   renders it. Delivery, streaming, tool cards and approvals are the framework's:
   the user types into the native composer, so no turn is ever pushed by hand.

@tyouter/dsh-notes README · Built with：Built with [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). The plugin was written in a
conversation with it — design, code, tests, the recorded clips and this README — and the same harness runs
its suites. Commits carry `Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>` as the record.
